{{!-- THE hero — quiet on purpose.

Headline is @site.title; the sub is one fixed line of positioning
copy (not @site.description) — no badges, no social proof, no
"just shipped" pill, no social rail on the card. Everything that
used to prove activity here now lives in partials/activity-feed.hbs,
right below.

Right: ONE square — the publication's own mark, and the film
behind it. The card sits at 1:1 until it is pressed, then morphs
to 16:9 and plays the intro; closing it returns the square. --}}

<section class="home-hero outer relative">
    {{!-- The backdrop is a PATTERN, not a photo: the crosshair
    blueprint (.home-hero-pattern) — an SVG tile used as a mask
    over a solid colour, so it recolours with the theme. --}}
    <div class="home-hero-pattern" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="orb" style="width: 420px; height: 420px; top: -120px; left: -140px;" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="orb" style="width: 360px; height: 360px; bottom: -80px; right: -100px; animation-delay: -4s;" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="home-hero-grid inner">

        <div class="home-hero-copy">

            <h1>{{@site.title}}</h1>
            <p class="home-hero-subtitle">{{t "Say Namaste to Salesforce!"}}</p>
            <p class="home-hero-sub">{{t "I'm upskilling myself for the AI era, one real build at a time — and documenting every step here instead of keeping it to myself. Open source, free to follow, and better with people building alongside me. Sign up to learn and build in public with me."}}</p>

            {{!-- The ask — compact --}}
            {{#if @site.members_enabled}}
                {{#unless @member}}
                    <form class="signup-form hero-signup is-compact" data-members-form="signup">
                        <div class="signup-row">
                            <input class="signup-input" data-members-email type="email" required
                                placeholder="{{t "you@work-email.com"}}" aria-label="{{t "Your email"}}" />
                            <button class="btn signup-btn" type="submit">
                                {{> "icons/mail"}} {{t "Follow along"}}
                            </button>
                        </div>
                        <p class="signup-note">{{t "Free forever · one email a week · unsubscribe in one click"}}</p>
                        <p class="signup-success">{{> "icons/check-circle"}} {{t "Almost in! Check your inbox and click the magic link."}}</p>
                        <p class="signup-error" data-members-error></p>
                    </form>
                {{else}}
                    <div class="home-hero-actions">
                        <a class="btn btn-lg" href="{{@site.url}}/courses/">{{> "icons/graduation-cap"}} {{t "Continue learning"}}</a>
                    </div>
                {{/unless}}
            {{else}}
                <div class="home-hero-actions">
                    <a class="btn btn-lg" href="{{@site.url}}/courses/">{{> "icons/graduation-cap"}} {{t "Browse courses"}}</a>
                </div>
            {{/if}}

            {{!-- Social handles — Ghost's own accounts (Admin →
            Settings → Social accounts) plus the theme's own link
            settings; each renders only when set, and the row
            disappears entirely when none are. Always shown, not
            gated on membership state like the ask above it. --}}
            <ul class="hero-social-row">
                {{#if @site.twitter}}
                    <li><a href="{{social_url type="twitter"}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="X">{{> "icons/x"}}</a></li>
                {{/if}}
                {{#if @site.facebook}}
                    <li><a href="{{social_url type="facebook"}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Facebook">{{> "icons/facebook"}}</a></li>
                {{/if}}
                {{#if @custom.social_youtube}}
                    <li><a href="{{@custom.social_youtube}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="YouTube">{{> "icons/youtube"}}</a></li>
                {{/if}}
                {{#if @custom.social_linkedin}}
                    <li><a href="{{@custom.social_linkedin}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="LinkedIn">{{> "icons/linkedin"}}</a></li>
                {{/if}}
                {{#if @custom.social_github}}
                    <li><a href="{{@custom.social_github}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="GitHub">{{> "icons/github"}}</a></li>
                {{/if}}
                {{#if @custom.social_instagram}}
                    <li><a href="{{@custom.social_instagram}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Instagram">{{> "icons/instagram"}}</a></li>
                {{/if}}
            </ul>
        </div>

        {{!-- Right: the publication cover, and the film behind it.

        The card rests at 1:1 showing the publication cover (Admin →
        Design → Publication cover) under a brand scrim. ONE toggle
        straddles its bottom edge: press it and the card morphs to
        16:9 and mounts the YouTube embed, press it again and the
        cover returns. The toggle floats OUTSIDE the frame on
        purpose — inside, it landed on YouTube's own controls.

        NOTHING is requested from YouTube until that first press, so
        a visitor who never plays the film meets no third-party
        frame, script or cookie. See assets/js/hero-video.js.

        The chips floating around the card are the publication's own
        most-used tags, not decoration invented here — they grow and
        change with the site instead of going stale.

        The film's address comes from Admin → Design → Site-wide →
        "Hero video". Empty, the card is simply the cover. --}}
        <div class="hero-feature">
            <div class="hero-feature-card{{#if @custom.hero_video}} has-video{{/if}}"
                {{#if @custom.hero_video}}data-hero-video="{{@custom.hero_video}}"{{/if}}>

                <div class="hero-feature-poster">
                    {{#if @site.cover_image}}
                        <img class="hero-feature-cover" src="{{img_url @site.cover_image size="l"}}" alt="" fetchpriority="high" />
                    {{else}}
                        {{!-- No cover set: the brand square stands in, so the
                        hero never renders as an empty grey box. --}}
                        <span class="hero-feature-grid" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="hero-feature-mark">
                            {{#if @site.icon}}
                                <img src="{{img_url @site.icon size="m"}}" alt="" fetchpriority="high" />
                            {{else}}
                                <img src="{{asset "images/ns-mark.svg"}}" alt="" fetchpriority="high" />
                            {{/if}}
                        </span>
                    {{/if}}

                    <span class="hero-feature-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </div>

                {{#if @custom.hero_video}}
                    {{!-- The embed lands here on press and is torn out again
                    on close, so a closed card holds no frame. --}}
                    <div class="hero-feature-stage" data-hero-stage></div>

                    {{!-- One control, two states — pressing it plays, pressing
                    it again brings the cover back. --}}
                    <button class="hero-feature-toggle" type="button"
                        data-hero-toggle
                        aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="hero-feature-disc" aria-hidden="true">
                            <svg class="i-play" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 7.5v9l7.5-4.5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
                            <svg class="i-close" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M7 7l10 10M17 7L7 17"/></svg>
                        </span>
                        <span class="hero-feature-toggle-label">
                            <span class="on-idle">{{t "Watch the intro"}}</span>
                            <span class="on-playing">{{t "Close"}}</span>
                        </span>
                    </button>
                {{/if}}
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>
